tion/math-academy-id "q-162646" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+({t}^{3}+1)\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n2t=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\operatorname{cos}⁡t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component ${t}^{3}+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162646/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162646"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162634/selection/12d00d8cbbf4a04c75ab1402693219a77b5a75fe9d62eb748da8bc882b535ddd" :answer/id #uuid "85640597-2642-5bef-80c4-48548dc1641b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{n\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162634/selection/44893c23f05e66e5e019ed914d57bc67e9de850732be0186aa8515e150e19846" :answer/id #uuid "33a9c6a4-e245-59a7-9b63-9783d82339fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162634/selection/947ea182cbe88a9a077a3a5b8a8314dd277a34fc772655914ed0030dcf8b2282" :answer/id #uuid "d9f39e27-372f-57a2-b3ff-8513e58fbf6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+2n\\pi " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "