er." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component ${e}^{1-t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $2\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+1$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )$, $t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,$ where $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi }{2}+n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162635/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162635"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162650/selection/31d3e65887c7dec91c6b628bb9d2d2f9598c7714cc0273f6866ed351bd5fe07c" :answer/id #uuid "c4fdcdc1-d699-5c14-8c66-66bf37c288ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162650/selection/b373265a004119846e223ebd2646ed5d1a9ab76460beed2ae2405ff030dc69d8" :answer/id #uuid "93e9cd34-4b71-5c8a-88b8-1ce9cbfe338e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162650/selection/9b1074132681bdfeab00dca99ba96b20e050f4aeafbb973622fac6267306a2ac" :answer/id #uuid "0c42b381-67e8-5ca1-9969-33980049add2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162650/selection/46c931a358d565c28807869bba82dd01e59ccf26d411034931757f1d53bcf122" :answer/id #uuid "36a593bd-0d3e-5235-a25d-ff86a66790a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi n}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162650/selection/409707feb39b45549eb01c3238a2f876a77d81bcc7d1cddfd63c85e12125d838" :answer/id #uuid "1ebcd1c8-e9bc-5aea-b717-b0ec07a21913" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\pi n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162650/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bfdf6073-475b-5acb-95f7-098cc0870664" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162650/selection/b373265a004119846e223ebd2646ed5d1a9ab76460beed2ae2405ff030dc69d8" :answer-field/choices ["q-162650/selection/31d3e65887c7dec91c6b628bb9d2d2f9598c7714cc0273f6866ed351bd5fe07c" "q-162650/selection/b373265a004119846e223ebd2646ed5d1a9ab76460beed2ae2405ff030dc69d8" "q-162650/selection/9b1074132681bdfeab00dca99ba96b20e050f4aeafbb973622fac6267306a2ac" "q-162650/selection/46c931a358d565c28807869bba82dd01e59ccf26d411034931757f1d53bcf122" "q-162650/selection/409707feb39b45549eb01c3238a2f876a77d81bcc7d1cddfd63c85e12125d838"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162650" :question/id #uuid "87c221f9-e693-5d8e-a2e1-2339b89f02d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-162650" :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=(1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3t))\\,i+3t\\,j+(2-{t}^{2})\\,k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne .\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression? You may assume that $n$ is an integer." :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡(3t)$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\n3t=\\pi n\\,⟹\\,t=\\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $3t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $2-{t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\\,t\\ne \\frac{\\pi n}{3},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-162650/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "553f7b9d-c387-59b0-a0d6-9624d012e414"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162650"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12350"] :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f(t) = \\left\\langle \\sqrt{t+3}, \\: t^3-t^2, \\: \\dfrac{1}{t+1}\\right\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{t+3}$ is $t \\in [-3,\\infty).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $t^3-t^2$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $\\dfrac{1}{t+1}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,-1)\\cup(-1,\\infty).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/9577ea515e58e4db49ee5a5ef9f923bc8b34e2dc232b904c956cc1b778141f14.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is $t \\in [-3,-1)\\cup(-1,\\infty).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12362"] :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f} (t) = \\ln{t} \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{1}{t-2} \\, \\mathbf{j} + e^{2t} \\, \\mathbf{k}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\ln{t}$ is $t \\in (0, \\infty).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\dfrac{1}{t-2}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,2)\\cup(2,\\infty).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $e^{2t}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/2a4931e8dc80192219736fc4dbc586ad2405bbb628d75bd0e17fa9616567d793.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is $t \\in (0,2)\\cup (2,\\infty).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-12455"] :question/problem "The domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f (t) = \\tan\\left(t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right) \\, \\mathbf i + t^3 \\,\\mathbf j + e^t \\,\\mathbf k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty,\\infty), \\quad t \\neq \\bbox[5pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\tan\\left(t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right)$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\nt+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nt =  \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $t^3$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $e^{t}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty,\\infty), \\quad t \\neq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
